From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] io_pipeline: pick the preview mode nearest the preview size

The preview mode is the one scoring best on frame rate and on how close
its area is to the preview's, but the area term was an integer division
and the best score started at 0. Any mode more than twice the preview's
area got a whole number of at least 2 taken off, scored below 0 and
could never be picked. On a phone whose smallest mode is 2624x1976 none
qualified, and the preview fell back to the 5248x3936 capture mode: 16
frames a second, and textures that took most of the GPU's memory, so the
first photo then failed with GL_OUT_OF_MEMORY and the
glCheckFramebufferStatus() assertion in gles2_debayer_process().

Divide in floating point and start from -INFINITY, so the nearest mode
always wins.

---
--- a/src/io_pipeline.c	2026-02-17 19:10:59.000000000 +0400
+++ b/src/io_pipeline.c	2026-10-15 19:47:03.764398211 +0400
@@ -612,7 +612,7 @@
                         mpcamera = mp_camera_new(state_io.camera);
                         state_io.mode_preview = NULL;
                         state_io.mode_capture = NULL;
-                        float score = 0;
+                        float score = -INFINITY;
                         int area_preview =
                                 state_io.preview_width * state_io.preview_height;
                         if (area_preview == 0) {
@@ -626,8 +626,8 @@
                                 int mode_area = state_io.camera->modes[m]->width *
                                                 state_io.camera->modes[m]->height;
                                 mscore += 1.0f -
-                                          (float)(ABS(mode_area - area_preview) /
-                                                  area_preview);
+                                          (float)ABS(mode_area - area_preview) /
+                                                  area_preview;
                                 if (mscore > score) {
                                         state_io.mode_preview =
                                                 state_io.camera->modes[m];
